    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between psyllium husk and psyllium seed powder?",
            "answer": "<p>Psyllium husk is the outer coat of the Plantago ovata seed it is the primary source of soluble dietary fibre. Psyllium seed powder includes the inner seed, which has lower fibre content and a different fermentation profile. AIWO Isabgol contains 100% psyllium husk not seed powder at 88.25g dietary fibre per 100g. Many cheaper market products blend the two or use mostly seed powder. Check for the fibre number, not just the name.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Isabgol just for constipation?",
            "answer": "<p>No this is the most common misunderstanding about psyllium husk.</p><p>Psyllium supports digestive regularity in both directions: it adds bulk and moisture to dry, hard stools (relieving constipation) and can firm loose stools by absorbing excess water in the colon (supporting diarrhoea). This is why it is classified as a bulk-forming fibre, not a laxative.</p><p>Beyond motility, psyllium is a prebiotic its soluble fibre ferments in the gut to feed Bifidobacterium and Lactobacillus, the two most studied beneficial gut bacteria families. It also supports healthy cholesterol levels as part of a daily fibre intake. Regularity is just one benefit of three.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can children take AIWO Isabgol?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes AIWO Isabgol is one of the few nutraceutical products with a specific child dosage on the label: <br/>5g (1 teaspoon) for children, compared to 10g (2 teaspoons) for adults. Always mix with a full glass of water and follow with an additional glass. Do not give to children under 6 without physician guidance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q6TUxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How should I take it so it doesn't clump?",
            "answer": "<p>Two rules: use a dry spoon, and drink it immediately after mixing.</p><p>Psyllium husk begins gelling within seconds of water contact. If you measure with a wet spoon, it will clump before you can mix it. If you let it sit too long after mixing, it becomes difficult to drink. Mix into a full glass of water, stir briefly, and drink before it thickens. Follow immediately with another glass of water for best results.</p><p>For cooking: mix into dry flour before adding water to your dough. It acts as a natural binding agent and does not affect taste.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WyBt4K": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I see a difference?",
